From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:52:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(harness-mock): what Claude Code would send when it
 resumes a projected session, without the binary

toolpath-harness-mock stands in for the agent the way toolpath-webmock stands
in for the model: claude::resume models Claude Code's loader (leaf, parentUuid
walk, roles, merges by message.id, parallel tool results) and check_api the
Messages API's rules. Tests: every projection into Claude Code resumes whole
except two pinned findings (opencode -> claude reaches 2 of 22 entries: every
assistant hangs off the first user turn; cursor -> claude has an unanswered
tool call); the pi parent-chain and copilot empty-errored-result bugs,
re-introduced in fixture copies, are caught; contract against the codex ->
claude webmock cassette. docs/mock-harness.md; pr/24.
